> Unitree, AgiBot, EngineAI, XPeng, Fourier, UBTECH, Kepler, MagicLab - none of them custom-engineer their actuators. This is likely very misleading! Most companies like Unitree (QDD M107, M118), Agibot, and LimX use proprietary in-house high-performing actuators.

While actuator companies provide a faster start in robot building, most advanced companies end up integrating actuators in-house, especially since actuators make up about 50% of the bill of materials.

@JulianSaks: "A humanoid robot is a collection of joints, each driven by an actuator. Most are rotary actuators - a brushless motor, a precision reducer, an encoder, a torque sensor, a set of bearings, and the..."

A research-led product needs a mindset shift in leadership and product teams. Understanding model capabilities and their trajectory is essential, and it only works if the internal team understands and can execute research.

Notably, the playbook is not guided by what the market wants today, as it may not be feasible. It is about finding the Model-Market Fit (MMF), which is also non-stationary due to changing model capabilities.

@oyhsu: "The most underrated skillset right now is the ability to build an effective research organization (recruiting the best research talent, giving them the resources they need). Seems obvious, but there’s very few places one would have developed this skillset over the last decade."
